<amended-claims-statement lang="EN">
<claims-statement>
<p id="pc0001" num="0001"> 66 </p>
<p id="pc0002" num="0002">Statement under Article 19(1) </p>
<p id="pc0003" num="0003">I am submitting an amendment under Articles 19 for my invention, and I would like to clarify the essence of my invention. My invention does not involve the mixing of any substances; rather, it is based on a special treatment of substances that results in the creation of a completely new substance with unique characteristics. This substance is not a mixture of any pre-existing substances, but rather a new entity in and of itself. </p>
<p id="pc0004" num="0004">This new substance is a "solid dispersion" (for example, in the form of a molecular dispersion) is thus a homogeneous or partially homogeneous system, which is not equivalent to a simple heterogeneous mixture of substances, and I am seeking a patent for its creation and use. I want to emphasize that no patents which propose mixing without treatment can intersect with my invention, as their innovation is focused on the creation of mixtures, while mine is centered around the creation of a new homogeneous system with radically different bioavailability and permeability properties. </p>
<p id="pc0005" num="0005">I hope this clarification helps you to understand the essence of my invention and the basis for my patent application. Thank you for your time and consideration. 
</p>
</claims-statement>
</amended-claims-statement>
